# Field-identical to rosbag2_interfaces/srv/Record as of rosbag2 0.34 (Rolling), deliberately.
#
# The recorder offers ~/record on every distro, and where the installed rosbag2_interfaces has
# this exact shape it is offered under that type, so a client written against stock rosbag2 can
# drive it. Jazzy's Record has no start_time and Kilted has no Record at all, so there the
# service is offered under this copy instead, with the same fields and the same behaviour.
# The recorder's CMake and dynrec.services make the same choice from the same evidence.
# See GetSubscribedTopics.srv for the reasoning behind copying rather than depending.

# Optional path where the new folder for recording will be created. If provided, it will override
# the storage_options.uri provided during construction. Empty by default.
string uri

# Timestamp in the future when to start recording.
# If empty or time in the past, recording starts immediately.
builtin_interfaces/Time start_time
---
# Return code. Returns 1 when recording is already running or in case of error, otherwise 0.
int32 return_code
# Error string. Empty if no error occurred.
string error_string
